  "summary": "REVSTEALER (tracked as REF2859) is an emerging Windows infostealer distributed through hijacked YouTube channels advertising free game cheats and through samples masquerading as recognizable software. It harvests browser, wallet, VPN, messaging and gaming-platform credentials, applies CIS locale exclusion and a ten-check sandbox scoring system, and uses Polygon smart-contract dead drops to retrieve fallback C2 addresses. Four C2-delivered modules (ProManager, WinUpdate, SoftManager, LockAppHost) extend it with phishing overlays, clipboard cryptocurrency swapping, SOCKS5 backconnect and XMRig deployment.",
